  "verdict": "allowed",
  "section": "106",
  "quote": "A landlord may require a tenant to pay a rent deposit with respect to a tenancy if the landlord does so on or before entering into the tenancy agreement.",
  "reason": "Section 106 permits a landlord to require a rent deposit on or before entering into the tenancy agreement, capped at one month's rent for a monthly tenancy, and requires it to be applied to the last rent period before the tenancy terminates."
}

